<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Sheikhdom of Bahrain</h1><p class="st-meta">1783 CE – 1971 CE · capital Manama</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Bahrain under the Al Khalifa and British protection, where the first oil on the Arab side of the Gulf was struck in 1932.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Al <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalifa">Khalifa</a>, a clan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bani-utbah">Bani Utbah</a> settled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zubarah">Zubarah</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-qatar">Qatar</a>, crossed to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-bahrain">Bahrain</a> in 1783 and drove out the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-madhkur">Al Madhkur</a> governor, who ruled for Persian-backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bushehr">Bushehr</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmed-al-fateh">Ahmad ibn Muhammad Al Khalifa</a>, known as al-Fateh, the Conqueror, became the first ruler of the islands.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-bahrain">Bahrain</a> lived on pearling, date farming and trade, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manama">Manama</a> as its port. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> ruling family governed a population that was largely Shi'a. Treaties with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> from 1820, culminating in the exclusive agreements of 1880 and 1892, made it a protected state. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isa-ibn-ali-al-khalifa">Isa bin Ali</a> to hand power to his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamad-ibn-isa-al-khalifa">Hamad</a> in 1923, Hamad and the British adviser <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-belgrave">Charles Belgrave</a>, from 1926, created courts, schools and a modern administration. Oil was struck in 1932.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> long claimed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-bahrain">Bahrain</a>, but a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> survey in 1970 found the people wanted independence. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> ended its protection and the State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahrain">Bahrain</a> became independent in August 1971 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isa-bin-salman-al-khalifa">Isa bin Salman Al Khalifa</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sheikhdom-of-bahrain.jpg" alt="Sheikhdom of Bahrain" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: Hoshie · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Bahrain_(1972%E2%80%932002).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1783 CE – 1971 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Manama</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ahmad al-Fateh, Isa bin Ali Al Khalifa, Isa bin Salman Al Khalifa</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam (Sunni rulers, Shi'a majority)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/bahrain">Bahrain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bahrain, Emirate of Bahrain, Al Khalifa Bahrain</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1877&amp;focus=sheikhdom-of-bahrain" aria-label="Sheikhdom of Bahrain on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6015 1220 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sheikhdom of Bahrain lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6335 1476L6562 1563M6335 1476L6237 1523M6335 1476L4997 651M6335 1476L6335 1476M6335 1476L6365 1504"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6562 1563h0M6237 1523h0M4997 651h0M6335 1476h0M6365 1504h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6335 1476h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6335 1476h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1877&amp;focus=sheikhdom-of-bahrain">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
